{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261024-c35e","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-24T00:00:00Z","claim":"The session's one full-suite run has no route into the answer, the verdict or the verdict doc. Step 4 builds the answer from the reviewers' reports, checks_executed is 'every check the reviewer ran' (answer.schema.json:21), and the Method line (signoff_core/result.py:101) and the verdict doc's 'Checks the reviewer executed' (signoff.py:1116) count only reviewer checks; the session may not form the verdict or edit findings. Before this slice a reviewer's full run carried a regression in as an executed finding. Raised by all three lenses (spec F1, correctness F1, seams F1).","finding":"f1:67aac180b0204025c389","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-24-e17-fix-round-1.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/SKILL.md","line":85,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/SKILL.md:85","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"aae51e91a00d323f009bcd0fdac72fe1481860206fab76d166aa95133da9a6e5","raised_by":"A","scenario":"A slice edits signoff.py so an untouched module (say test_sheet) goes red. Each reviewer runs only the narrow modules it guesses are relevant and reports clean with those checks listed. The session's Step 3.5 full run shows the failure, but nothing turns it into a finding: record-answer accepts the clean answer, the verdict is computed signed off and the card moves with the suite red. If the session instead merges its run into checks_executed, the verdict doc credits a session check to the independent reviewer and a reviewer that ran nothing passes Step 4 rule 3 on it. REVIEW.md bar: 'a failing check that CI would catch' is MAJOR.","seq":6,"severity":"MAJOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"8223bba5cb53d86afcd81bb8a8d8a517608ce11c","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261024-c35e","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-24T00:00:00Z","claim":"The narrowest-command rule covers only proving or refuting 'a finding'; the removed 'Run tests' was the only positive instruction to execute anything when there is no finding. (spec F2)","finding":"f1:44ddcff2a2bc4c62f996","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-24-e17-fix-round-1.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff.py","line":533,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff.py:533","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"6853c0fd0af28c25821ff0b162c19d24390ad41150c0ce31c484f643fd91c849","raised_by":"A","scenario":"A LEAN review where all three lenses find nothing and each runs nothing: checks_executed is empty, Step 4 rule 3 refuses the answer as answer_invalid, and the lenses are re-sent, costing back time the slice meant to save.","seq":7,"severity":"MINOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"8223bba5cb53d86afcd81bb8a8d8a517608ce11c","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261024-c35e","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-24T00:00:00Z","claim":"The mandate states as fact that the reviewing session runs the full test command once, for every run; nothing enforces or records it, and SKILL.md Step 3.5 keeps a 'nothing is runnable' path where no full run happens. (spec F3, correctness F2, seams F5)","finding":"f1:2bd5a818bdfbacfc6c82","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-24-e17-fix-round-1.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff.py","line":531,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff.py:531","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"9992ea786e091917140437496a6371205739dc53fd40397ddd285b19edf37f87","raised_by":"A","scenario":"In a repo with no runnable suite, or when the session skips Step 3.5, every reviewer defers to a full run that never occurs; the commands they named go unrun and nothing in the result shows the gap.","seq":8,"severity":"MINOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"8223bba5cb53d86afcd81bb8a8d8a517608ce11c","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261024-c35e","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-24T00:00:00Z","claim":"Nothing orders the session's full run against the reviewers' narrow runs, though the plan's C-25 constraint says suites run side by side fail on a missing jsonschema from the nested uv run; Step 3 launches the fleet before Step 3.5 and the mandate does not warn reviewers. (spec F4, correctness F3, seams F4)","finding":"f1:e50fbb41a06dfbada96b","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-24-e17-fix-round-1.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/SKILL.md","line":85,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/SKILL.md:85","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"ae1ed180dfa39983f3068a17d9aeda37d4a0bbd4b0058e7bd0e2c8cf013866dd","raised_by":"A","scenario":"The session runs the core suite while a reviewer runs one adapter module through uv run --with jsonschema==4.25.1; the module fails on the import and the reviewer raises a false executed failure, or the session's full run goes red spuriously.","seq":9,"severity":"MINOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"8223bba5cb53d86afcd81bb8a8d8a517608ce11c","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261024-c35e","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-24T00:00:00Z","claim":"Nothing tells the session what to do with a full-suite command a reviewer names instead of running; Step 3.5 runs 'the project's full test command' and never reads the reports for named commands or says who runs a different one. (seams F2)","finding":"f1:cc08ab2ba10e4d893233","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-24-e17-fix-round-1.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/SKILL.md","line":85,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/SKILL.md:85","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"88a4e0eaaf2f7c43fa672730cba5e5e2b5c482ac245bc5765165ac070e1cd55d","raised_by":"A","scenario":"A reviewer suspects a regression in the codex adapter suite and names its command without running it; the session runs only the core suite; the finding reaches Step 4 as reasoned and the named command is never run.","seq":10,"severity":"MINOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"8223bba5cb53d86afcd81bb8a8d8a517608ce11c","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
